Every Ladybird process now ignores SIGPIPE from the start, and the
programs that Core::Process spawns get SIGPIPE’s default action back.
Chromium does both: SetupSignalHandlers() in content_main.cc ignores
SIGPIPE in every process, and base::LaunchProcess() resets each signal
to its default in the child (ResetChildSignalHandlersToDefaults()).
WebKit’s AuxiliaryProcess::platformInitialize() ignores SIGPIPE in its
auxiliary processes on Unix. That’s from reading the source.
